<title>POLAND: COMPUTERLAND SETS STOCK OPTION AT PLN 1.</title>
<headline>COMPUTERLAND SETS STOCK OPTION AT PLN 1.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish software firm Computerland SA has priced two stock-option issues for management and employees at one zloty per share, the company said in an abbreviated version of its issue prospectus.</p>
<p>The firm is offering 207,897 shares to management and 66,000 shares to other top employees.</p>
<p>ComputerLand, whose stock closed on the Warsaw bourse on Tuesday at 95 zlotys, currently has 4,862,760 shares outstanding.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
